markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Lesson 4: Optimization in Action</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lesson 6</div>

<p>This lesson prepares you to teach one curriculum lesson. Students have been reasoning step by step with pseudocode and functions. Now they turn that same precision toward a new kind of problem: not just "what are the steps," but "how do you know when you've found a good answer."</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 6:</b> Optimization</p>
<a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_6_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 6</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this lesson, you'll:</b></p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">&bull; Work through a hill-climbing simulation, the same reasoning process students use to search for a good solution step by step</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">&bull; Try an unplugged thermostat activity, grounding the concept in something physical before it's code</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">&bull; Get clear yourself on local vs. global optimum, a distinction worth having solid before a student asks you to explain it on the spot</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">&bull; See where this sets up the rest of the unit: optimization is the first real preview of how AI systems search for answers, not just follow fixed rules</p>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #222222; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
<p><b>&#128161; Notice as you explore:</b> how easy it is to mistake "a good answer" for "the best answer." That confusion is exactly what the local-vs-global-optimum distinction exists to untangle, and it's worth feeling the confusion yourself once before you have to clear it up for a student.</p>
</div>

<hr>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 6px; margin-top: 24px; max-width: 700px;">
